  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Maximum&nbsp;l&nbsp;value should be equal to&nbsp;n&minus;1&nbsp;and it cannot be equal to&nbsp;n.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo></math> It can be upto <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and&nbsp;</p><p>Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math></p><p>for&nbsp;(a)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> (correct),</p><p>for (b)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;(correct),</p><p>(c)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;(not correct),</p><p>(d)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;(correct),</p>"
